{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefectClosedForm"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.canonicalCandidate_passes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.canonicalCandidate_passes","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**The gate is satisfiable (non-vacuous).** The proved cubic `n144C` is itself a passing\ncandidate, so the specification is consistent — it is not vacuously unsatisfiable. The open question\n(G1) is whether a *geometric* (Seifert–CS) index realizes this `a₂`; the gate is what such a\nconstruction would be tested against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.canonicalCandidate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.canonicalCandidate","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The framework's own proved cubic, packaged as a candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_forces_sign_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_forces_sign_flip","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**The falsifiable n = 7 discriminant.** Any index passing G2 *must* exhibit the exact sign flip:\n`a₂` is positive at rank 6 and negative at rank 7. A candidate geometric index whose 2nd heat-kernel\ncoefficient does not change sign between ranks 6 and 7 is **refuted**. This is the decisive,\nparameter-free teeth of the gate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_forces_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_forces_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L50-L54","doc":"**Passing forces the closed-form cubic.** Any index passing G2 has\n`a₂(n) = −n(n−1)(2n−13)` — the program's q₀-free target (1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.defectGate_unique","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L44-L48","doc":"**The gate pins the coefficient uniquely.** Two indices that pass G2 have identical 2nd\nheat-kernel coefficients — the gate leaves no free constant to tune. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.PassesDefectGate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.PassesDefectGate","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L40-L42","doc":"**The G2 defect gate.** A candidate passes iff its cleared 2nd heat-kernel coefficient matches\nthe proved defect cubic `144·C(n)` (`n144C`) at every rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate.a₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate.a₂","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The cleared 2nd heat-kernel coefficient `144·a₂(n)` at rank `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneG2Gate.HeatKernelCandidate","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneG2Gate.lean#L32-L38","doc":"A **candidate equivariant index**, abstracted by its cleared 2nd heat-kernel coefficient\n`a₂ : ℤ → ℤ` (the `144·`-cleared coefficient at rank `n`, in `n144C`'s normalization). The geometric\ncontent — the actual Seifert–Chern–Simons index — is **G1** (owner-gated DG); this carrier is the\nfalsifiable *interface* the program gates on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}